e87n-display for Debian
======================

This architecture-independent Python package targets the EdgePi E87N and
requires the board's NV3007 framebuffer and backlight kernel support.
The kernel remains the default fan controller. `fan test LEVEL SECONDS` is a
root-only, bounded diagnostic: it briefly requests a thermal cooling level and
restores the previous level; it is not a persistent manual mode. The 428x142
screen shows kernel mode, cooling level and PWM percentage only; it deliberately
does not display tachometer RPM. No provisioning, account,
network, firmware or kernel installation is performed by this package.

Commands:
  e87nctl status
  e87nctl doctor
  e87nctl fan status
  e87nctl fan test 1 5
  e87nctl acceleration status
  e87nctl display brightness 20
  e87nctl display screen thermal
  e87nctl display theme dark
  e87nctl display rotation on
  e87nctl display rotation-seconds 3
  e87nctl display pages overview,cpu,memory,thermal,fan,network,traffic,storage
  e87nctl display off
  e87nctl display on

Display settings: /etc/e87n/display.json
Module configuration: /etc/modules-load.d/e87n-display.conf
Both are dpkg conffiles. Use --force-confdef --force-confold with unattended
dpkg upgrades when existing local settings must take precedence.

Themes are dark, aurora and light colour skins over the same eight page layouts.
Pages are overview, cpu, memory, thermal, fan, network, traffic and storage.
Fan and storage are skipped during automatic rotation when their telemetry is absent.
Automatic page rotation is disabled by default; enable it with `e87nctl display
rotation on` and choose a 2-60 second interval with `rotation-seconds`.

The service e87n-display.service is enabled at installation, respecting
administrator disable/mask choices on upgrades. Image builds must supply
an executable /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d returning 101 to inhibit activation.
An ordinary image chroot has no running systemd. The package neither starts
hardware directly nor creates or replaces policy-rc.d.

Removal stops the display and preserves conffiles; purge removes the package's
conffiles and helper state. Other board data and administrator overrides
are not recursively deleted. Service errors do not block package configuration;
inspect systemctl status e87n-display.service and its journal after boot.
